<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><ncx xmlns="http://www.daisy.org/z3986/2005/ncx/" version="2005-1" xml:lang="en"><head><meta name="dtb:uid" content="urn:uuid:d58113b6-87d1-52b7-803d-02d7e302b94f"/><meta name="dtb:depth" content="2"/><meta name="dtb:totalPageCount" content="0"/><meta name="dtb:maxPageNumber" content="0"/></head><docTitle><text>The War on Everyday Machines</text></docTitle><navMap><navPoint id="nav-1" playOrder="1"><navLabel><text>From remote commands to stocked shelves</text></navLabel><content src="text/reader-guide.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-2" playOrder="2"><navLabel><text>Evidence, models and the limits of this edition</text></navLabel><content src="text/method.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-3" playOrder="3"><navLabel><text>The power to change a temperature</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch001.xhtml"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-4" playOrder="4"><navLabel><text>The day supermarket freezers became a target</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#chapter-1"/><navPoint id="nav-5" playOrder="5"><navLabel><text>Three weeks, and an explanation that changed</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-three-weeks-and-an-explanation-that-changed"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-6" playOrder="6"><navLabel><text>A freezer also has a way to generate heat</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-a-freezer-also-has-a-way-to-generate-heat"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-7" playOrder="7"><navLabel><text>The tempting shortcut of a known vulnerability</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-the-tempting-shortcut-of-a-known-vulnerability"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-8" playOrder="8"><navLabel><text>A dramatic temperature needs a precise definition</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-a-dramatic-temperature-needs-a-precise-definition"/></navPoint><navPoint id="nav-9" playOrder="9"><navLabel><text>The hourly report may smooth away the event</text></navLabel><content src="text/ch002.xhtml#c1-